/*
# Combobox

Filter-as-you-type over a collection: a text field owning a **query** plus a
dismissable option list owning a **choice** — a derived selection over data.
Composition, not invention: `TextInput` for the entry, the `Menu` machinery for
the list (overlay, raise, light-dismiss, Escape closes — the whole dismissal
discipline rides along), and the matches are a derived collection — a
constraint over the items array, so the live match count is free and no
rendered row is ever scanned.

    Combobox [ width = 240, placeholder = "Assignee",
        items = { app.people }, input(v: object) { app.assignee = v } ]

- **Items are members** (the selection model's currency): records — shown by
  their `label` (or `id`) — or plain strings. `value` holds the chosen member;
  `input(v)` is the delivery seam: the default writes `value`, a use-site
  override redirects and the attribute stays untouched.
- **Typing filters live** (case-insensitive substring); opening without typing
  shows the full list (the disclosure-button path). Picking echoes the label
  into the field and closes; editing again re-filters from the new text.
- **Keyboard**: arrows rove the list (the Menu rover), Enter picks the roved
  row — or, when none is roved, the first match of what was typed (the
  type-then-Enter path); over the whole list it keeps the choice already made;
  Escape closes the list (then a second Escape leaves the control — the
  focus-scope ascent). The list is never a tab stop of its own.
- The list is a collection like any other — bind 100k options and
  `virtualize` applies to it the same way (via the Menu it composes).

```declare
App [ width = 320, height = 160, picked: string = "",
    people: array = { ["Ada Lovelace", "Grace Hopper", "Alan Turing", "Barbara Liskov"] },
    Combobox [ x = 20, y = 20, width = 240, placeholder = "Assignee",
        items = { app.people },
        input(v: object) { app.picked = "" + v }
        ],
    Text [ x = 20, y = 80, text = { app.picked == "" ? "—" : app.picked } ]
    ]
```

## items
The options, as **members**: records — shown by their `label`, else `id` — or plain
strings. The currency of the selection model, so whatever you put in is what comes back
out of `input`.

## value
The **chosen member**, not the typed text — the whole record when you supplied records.
`null` until something is picked. Standalone the combobox owns it; constrained, override
`input` beside it.

## input()
**Where the choice goes.** Receives the chosen member. The default writes `value`; an
override redirects it and leaves the attribute untouched.

## placeholder
The entry's placeholder text while empty.

## purpose
What the choice is — `country`, `region`, `name` — given to the entry, so autofill and a
password manager recognise the field, and a phone brings up the keyboard that suits it. Text
that arrives whole and names exactly one item, as autofill's does, picks that item.

## query
What the user has typed since the last pick. **Not the value** — the draft that filters
the list.

## matches
The filtered options, as a **derived collection**: a constraint over `items`, so the
live match count is free and **no rendered row is ever scanned**. Case-insensitive
substring against each member's label.

## matchCount
How many options currently match — read it straight, rather than counting list rows,
which is both wrong under virtualization and refused by the compiler.

## filtering
Whether the user has typed since the last pick. False means a bare disclosure, which
**shows the whole list** rather than filtering against a stale query — the difference
between clicking the chevron and typing.

## labelOf()
How a member is displayed: a record's `label`, else its `id`, else the value itself.
Override to display members your own way.

## open()
Opens the full list unfiltered — the disclosure-button path.

## toggle()
Opens the list, or closes it if it is already open.

## closeList()
Closes the list without picking.

## pickIndex()
Picks the *n*th current match: echoes its label into the entry, closes the list, and
delivers the member through `input`. The index is into `matches`, never into `items`.

## list
The option list — **a `Menu` created at the app layer on first open**, not a child of
the combobox, so it paints over everything rather than only over later siblings. All the
overlay behaviour arrives with it: light dismiss, Escape, the arrow rover, the viewport
flip, the long-list scroll.

## ensureList()
Creates the shared list on first use and wires its delivery back to `pickIndex`.

## syncList()
Pushes the current matches into the list — called on every keystroke.

## listShown()
Whether the list is currently up.

## listRoved()
Whether the keyboard rover is sitting on a row. **This is what makes Enter mean two
things**: pick the roved row when there is one, else take the first match of what was
typed — the type-then-Enter path. With nothing typed, Enter keeps the choice already made.

## height
From the theme's `comboboxHeight` (30 by default), and at least 44 on a touch-first
device, a finger's target.

## accessibilityExpanded
Whether the list is open — what a screen reader hears as the combobox expanded or collapsed.

## accessibilityLabel
The caption of a `Field` around it, else the `placeholder`, unless the use site names the combobox — its name to a screen reader, carried by
the field inside, which is what holds the focus.

## fieldValue
Follows `value`, the chosen member: what `required` and `validate` judge (see `ValueControl`).
*/

include [ "valuecontrol.declare", "menu.declare" ]

use [ Menu ]

class Combobox extends ValueControl [
    // a field and the list it drops: a combobox, expanded while its list is open;
    // the field inside is the text field a screen reader edits

    accessibilityRole = combobox,
    accessibilityLabel = { provided("fieldLabel", "") || placeholder },
    accessibilityExpanded = { this.listShown() },
    width = 220,

    // one Tab stop: the entry is the stop, the combobox around it is not

    focusable = false,
    height = { app.touchFirst ? Math.max(44, provided("theme").comboboxHeight) : provided("theme").comboboxHeight },

    // ── the surface ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    items: array = null,        // the option members: records or strings
    value: object = null,       // the choice — the chosen member, or null
    fieldValue = { value },
    placeholder: string = "",

    // what the choice is — `country`, `region` — so autofill and a phone's
    // keyboard treat the entry as that field; the entry carries it

    purpose: InputPurpose = text,

    // the query — what the user has typed since last pick; `filtering` is
    // false until they type, so a bare disclosure shows the whole list

    query: string = "",
    filtering: boolean = false,

    labelOf(m: object) -> string {
        if (m == null) return ""
        if (typeof m == "object") return "" + ((m as any).label ?? (m as any).id ?? "")
        return "" + m
        },

    // ── the derived collection: filtering is a data derivation — the count
    //    rides along, nothing scans rendered rows ───────────────────────────

    matches: array = { !filtering || query == ""
        ? (items ?? [])
        : (items ?? []).filter((m) => this.labelOf(m).toLowerCase().includes(query.toLowerCase())) },
    matchCount: number = { (matches ?? []).length },

    // ── the delivery seam ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    input(v: object) { value = v },
    focusField() { Focus.focus(entry) },

    pickIndex(i: number) {
        const m = (this.matches ?? [])[i]
        if (m === undefined) return
        filtering = false
        this.closeList()
        input(m)
        },

    // ── the list is a Menu made beside the combobox, lazily at first open —
    //    the way Menu makes its own cascade — so it opens in the overlay
    //    layer of the combobox's context (a window's, in a window) and paints
    //    over everything there. Its items are pushed on each keystroke, as
    //    Menu drives its own cascade child ───────────────────────────────────

    //    (View-typed attribute + any-seam driving — Menu members are invisible
    //    across files, the seam menu.declare itself uses)

    list: View? = null,

    ensureList() {
        if (list != null) return
        // a list of choices: a listbox of options, as a combobox's is everywhere
        list = (this.parent as View).createView("Menu", ({ accessibilityRole: "listbox", asList: true }))
        const m = this.list as any
        m.typeahead = false                       // its letters are the entry's
        m.takesFocus = false                      // the focus stays in the entry, which names the row
        m.picked = (id) => this.pickIndex(parseInt(id))
        },

    syncList() {
        this.ensureList()
        const m = this.list as any
        m.minWidth = this.width        // at least the field's width; a long label may widen it
        m.items = (this.matches ?? []).map((o, i) => ({ id: "" + i, label: this.labelOf(o), selected: o === value }))
        },

    closeList() { if (list != null) (this.list as any).close() },
    listShown() -> boolean { return this.list != null && (this.list as any).shown === true },
    listRoved() -> boolean { return this.list != null && (this.list as any).activeRow != null },

    open() {
        filtering = false
        this.syncList()
        const m = this.list as any
        m.openFor(this)
        },
    toggle() { if (this.listShown()) this.closeList(); else this.open() },

    // ── the entry: a TextInput owning the draft; each edit re-derives the
    //    matches and shows the list ─────────────────────────────────────────

    entry: TextInput [ x = 0, y = 0,
        width = { classroot.width },

        // what it shows derives from the choice — the query while one is typed,
        // else the chosen member's label — so a value set from outside (a
        // saved address's country) shows as surely as one picked here

        text = { classroot.filtering ? classroot.query : classroot.labelOf(classroot.value) },
        height = { classroot.height },
        placeholder = { classroot.placeholder },
        purpose = { classroot.purpose },

        // the field is what a screen reader edits, so it carries the combobox's name

        accessibilityLabel = { classroot.accessibilityLabel },

        // and its error and its being required; leaving the field (not for
        // the list) is leaving the combobox

        accessibilityError = { classroot.error },
        stroke = { stroke(1, classroot.error != "" ? provided("theme").error : this.focused ? provided("theme").accent : provided("theme").line) },
        accessibilityRequired = { classroot.accessibilityRequired },
        onBlur() { if (classroot.judgeOn == "leave" && !classroot.listShown()) classroot.judged = true },
        accessibilityActiveItem = { classroot.list == null ? null : (classroot.list as any).accessibilityActiveItem },
        focusable = { !classroot.disabled },
        onInput(t: string) {
            // text that arrives whole (autofill, a paste) and names exactly one
            // item picks it; typing that passes through an item's name does not,
            // so "Ann" on the way to "Anna" stays a query
            const whole = t.length - classroot.query.length > 1
            const exact = whole ? (classroot.items ?? []).filter((m) => classroot.labelOf(m).toLowerCase() == t.toLowerCase()) : []
            if (exact.length == 1) {
                classroot.query = "" + t
                classroot.filtering = false
                classroot.closeList()
                classroot.input(exact[0])
                return
                }
            classroot.query = "" + t
            classroot.filtering = true
            classroot.syncList()
            if (!classroot.listShown()) (classroot.list as any).openFor(classroot)
            },
        onEnter() {
            if (!classroot.listShown()) { classroot.open(); return }
            // the roved row picks through the Menu's own Enter; unroved, Enter
            // takes the first match of what was typed — the type-then-Enter
            // path — and over the whole list keeps the choice already made
            if (classroot.listRoved()) return
            if (classroot.filtering) { classroot.pickIndex(0); return }
            const at = (classroot.matches ?? []).indexOf(classroot.value)
            if (at >= 0) classroot.pickIndex(at)
            else classroot.closeList()
            }
        ],

    // the disclosure — a drawn chevron over the entry's right edge; tap
    // opens (the touch path: tap opens, tap picks)

    disc: View [ width = 22,
        x = { classroot.width - this.width - 2 },
        y = center,
        height = { classroot.height - 4 },
        onClick() { classroot.toggle() },

        // The disclosure chevron, from the shared set. The wrapper keeps the
        // 22px tap area (the touch path: tap opens, tap picks) — an icon is a
        // mark, not a hit target, so the two stay separate objects.

        mark: ChevronIcon [ iconSize = 13, ink = { provided("theme").textMuted }, x = center, y = center ]
        ]

    // (the Menu machinery arrives whole with the app-level instance above:
    //  overlay, raise, backdrop light-dismiss, Escape, the arrow rover, the
    //  viewport flip, the long-list scroll — the id is the match index,
    //  identity stays the member's)
    ]
